content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-110 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-24020; drive-end bearing housing",
  "priority": "P1",
  "stop_equipment_now": true,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Drive-end bearing housing temperature is 92°C and rising. The applicable HF-300 limits are normal up to 70°C, alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C. The reading is therefore 22°C above the normal limit, 12°C above alarm and 2°C above trip; the 90°C trip limit governs the immediate condition. Stop the pump now if it has not already tripped. Because it is also above the 80°C alarm limit, SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The reported vibration of 4.0 mm/s falls within the HF-300 Zone B range of 2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, labelled 'Long-term operation', when assessed as bearing-housing RMS velocity. It is below the 4.5 mm/s boundary for Zone C restricted operation and below the 7.1 mm/s boundary for Zone D. It is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone, so the vibration-based SSP-07 requirement for immediate stopping and reliability-engineer notification before restart is not currently triggered. The immediate shutdown decision instead arises from the temperature trip exceedance.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No numerical bearing-noise limit is supplied. However, the manual identifies bearing wear and misalignment as possible causes of high bearing temperature and requires both bearings to be replaced as a pair when either shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported noise and high temperature therefore support pair replacement rather than replacement of only the drive-end bearing.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or damage — assess first because bearing wear is listed for both high bearing temperature and high vibration, and the bearing is also reported noisy.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment — listed as a probable cause of both high bearing temperature and high vibration; check alignment.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing — listed as a probable cause of high bearing temperature; check grease quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; inspect the impeller.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Cavitation — listed as a probable cause of high vibration; check NPSH.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Immediately stop P-110 if it is still running and establish whether the 90°C temperature trip has operated. Execute the work as P1 because the bearing temperature is above the manufacturer's 80°C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, electrically isolate and apply lock-out/tag-out at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; obtain a line-break permit; and drain and vent the pump first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before any lift of the back pull-out assembly, prepare a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment. The assembly weighs 68 kg, exceeding the 25 kg SSP-07 threshold, and the manual expressly requires lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "With the pump safely isolated, investigate the listed causes: check grease quantity, inspect the bearings and impeller, check alignment and check NPSH. Record inspection findings before finalising any additional repair scope.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair because noise and high temperature are reported: fit one HF3-512 drive-end bearing 6312-C3 and one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble using the Table 5 torques for lightly oiled threads: tighten M12 bearing-housing bolts to 85 Nm. If the casing is opened, fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket and tighten M16 casing bolts to 210 Nm. If the M24 impeller nut is disturbed, tighten it to 160 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Achieve parallel offset of 0.05 mm and angular alignment of 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "During return to service, measure bearing-housing vibration as mm/s RMS and compare temperature and vibration with the HF-300 limits. Normal bearing-housing temperature is up to 70°C, with alarm at 80°C and trip at 90°C. Vibration Zone C is restricted operation requiring planned maintenance; Zone D indicates likely damage and requires the pump to be stopped. If highest-zone vibration occurs, stop immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace as part of the bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as part of the bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; conditional part, with one required whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Over-temperature response: keep the pump stopped if it has tripped, or stop it immediately if still running at 92°C and rising. Raise and execute a priority-1 work order within the shift because the temperature exceeds the 80°C alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Isolation controls for work inside the pump: electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Lifting controls for the 68 kg back pull-out assembly: a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and certified lifting equipment are required because the load exceeds 25 kg.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vibration emergency control: the current 4.0 mm/s reading is not in the highest zone, but if vibration enters Zone D, stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement as a pair: standard labour allowance is 6.0 hours with 2 technicians, equivalent to 12 technician-hours.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: allow 1.5 hours with 1 technician when required because the motor or bearing housing has been moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If both bearing replacement and alignment are performed, the listed standard-time subtotal is 7.5 task hours and 13.5 technician-hours. Table 6 provides no separate allowances for diagnosis, isolation, lifting or any additional casing, impeller or seal repairs.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C09",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Mechanical-seal selection, if seal work is added: the manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, but Service Bulletin SB-2026-014, issued 14 March 2026, prohibits HF3-450 on HF-300 pumps from serial HF3-22000 upward and requires pre-set cartridge seal HF3-450B. P-110's serial HF3-24020 is within that range, so HF3-450B governs for this asset; do not fit HF3-450. No sleeve measurement is needed to set the pre-set cartridge seal.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal-gland torque, if seal work is added: Table 5 gives 25 Nm for M10 seal gland nuts, whereas SB-2026-014 specifies 30 Nm for HF3-450B and identifies 25 Nm as the former value. Because this pump is in the bulletin's serial range, use 30 Nm for an HF3-450B installation. This seal-specific decision does not change the 85 Nm Table 5 torque for the M12 bearing-housing bolts.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "Does the reported 4.0 mm/s vibration represent RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing? Figure 3's zones apply specifically to mm/s RMS measured on bearing housings, so the Zone B classification is provisional until the measurement method and location are confirmed. [C07]",
    "Has the 90°C temperature trip already operated, and is P-110 currently stopped? The supplied documents do not specify who must authorise restart after an over-temperature trip; confirm the operational restart hold and approval. [C02,C15]",
    "What is the correct grease type and specified grease quantity, and what is the approved step-by-step bearing removal and installation method? The supplied manual excerpt requires a grease-quantity check and pair replacement but does not provide those details. [C09,C10]",
    "Will bearing access require the casing to be opened or the impeller or mechanical seal to be disturbed? This determines whether the conditional gasket and fastener steps apply and whether the serial-specific HF3-450B seal and 30 Nm gland torque must be added to the scope. [C05,C11,C13]",
    "What fluid and line service does P-110 have? Chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required for work on chemically dosed lines, but the evidence identifies only P-101 to P-106 on the filtered-water line as sodium-hypochlorite dosed; applicability to P-110 cannot be settled from the supplied evidence. [C15,C16]",
    "What do the inspections reveal about bearing wear, grease quantity, alignment, impeller condition and NPSH? These findings are needed to confirm the root cause and determine whether parts or repairs beyond the bearing pair and conditional casing gasket are required. [C09]"
  ]
}
